(LST2-68 — `but if` attaches to the INNERMOST iteration of a grid and its
 condition may reference every loop variable, since every loop is outside
 the conditional. The manual's own diagonal example: the alternative fires
 on exactly the three cells where left equals right.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox LST2-68.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   diag
   1-2
   1-3
   2-1
   diag
   2-3
   3-1
   3-2
   diag
)
To pair of a number called left and a number called right.
  print "{left}-{right}".

'pair' of each left from [1, 2, 3] and each right from [1, 2, 3], but if left is right print "diag".
